HEAD(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    head - print the beginning of a file

SYNOPSIS
    head [-n count | -c count] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the first ten lines by default. -n selects a line count; -c selects
    a byte count. Counts must be nonnegative. -n5 and -c5 are accepted.
    With no files or a file named -, reads stdin.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), man(1), index(7)
